Begin Exploring Related Columns
Below are the main tables/columns that matter for answering  
“what % of participants have an ICD‑10‑CM diagnosis in the L70, L20, L40 or L80 families (including all their descendants)” in the synthetic OMOP data.

Relevant columns and why

• `cms_synthetic_patient_data_omop.concept`  
  – `concept_id`: unique key used everywhere in OMOP.  
  – `concept_code`: holds the ICD‑10‑CM code such as “L70”, “L70.0”, …  
  – `vocabulary_id`: restrict to ‘ICD10CM’ so we look only at ICD‑10‑CM concepts.  
  – `standard_concept`: whether the concept is standard (“S”) or non‑standard; we keep standard only.

• `cms_synthetic_patient_data_omop.concept_ancestor`  
  – `ancestor_concept_id`, `descendant_concept_id`: already‑built hierarchy table.  
  – Filtering on `ancestor_concept_id` = the standard concept for L70, L20, L40, L80 instantly gives every descendant (including itself).

• `cms_synthetic_patient_data_omop.condition_occurrence`  
  – `person_id`: who had the condition.  
  – `condition_concept_id`: the STANDARD concept used in the row (already mapped from source by SynPUF).  
  – We count distinct `person_id` whose `condition_concept_id` is in the descendant sets created above.

• `cms_synthetic_patient_data_omop.person`  
  – `person_id`: universe of participants; lets us compute the denominator.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
Ten exploratory → final SQLs
(each limited to 20 rows so you can run them safely while exploring)

```sql
-- 1. Look up the root ICD‑10‑CM concepts (should return one row each)
SELECT concept_id, concept_code, concept_name, standard_concept
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cms_synthetic_patient_data_omop.concept`
WHERE vocabulary_id = 'ICD10CM' AND concept_code IN ('L70','L20','L40','L80');
```

```sql
-- 2. Inspect all ICD‑10‑CM codes that start with L70 (acne family)
SELECT concept_id, concept_code, concept_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cms_synthetic_patient_data_omop.concept`
WHERE vocabulary_id = 'ICD10CM' AND concept_code LIKE 'L70%';
```

```sql
-- 3. Grab a sample of descendant concept_ids for the acne ancestor (replace 12345 by real id from step 1)
SELECT descendant_concept_id
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cms_synthetic_patient_data_omop.concept_ancestor`
WHERE ancestor_concept_id = 12345  -- L70 concept_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Join to get human‑readable acne descendant names
SELECT c.descendant_concept_id, d.concept_code, d.concept_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cms_synthetic_patient_data_omop.concept_ancestor` AS c
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.cms_synthetic_patient_data_omop.concept`     AS d
  ON d.concept_id = c.descendant_concept_id
WHERE c.ancestor_concept_id = 12345       -- L70
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Sample condition records mapped to any acne descendant concept
SELECT co.person_id, co.condition_start_date, co.condition_concept_id
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cms_synthetic_patient_data_omop.condition_occurrence` AS co
WHERE co.condition_concept_id IN (
      SELECT descendant_concept_id
      FROM `bigquery-public-data.cms_synthetic_patient_data_omop.concept_ancestor`
      WHERE ancestor_concept_id = 12345 )     -- L70
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. How many unique participants have at least one acne (L70*) condition?
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT person_id) AS acne_participants
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cms_synthetic_patient_data_omop.condition_occurrence`
WHERE condition_concept_id IN (
      SELECT descendant_concept_id
      FROM `bigquery-public-data.cms_synthetic_patient_data_omop.concept_ancestor`
      WHERE ancestor_concept_id = 12345 );     -- L70
```

```sql
-- 7. Denominator: total number of participants in the synthetic cohort
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT person_id) AS total_participants
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cms_synthetic_patient_data_omop.person`;
```

```sql
-- 8. Wrap the previous logic into one query returning counts for the four ancestors
WITH roots AS (
  SELECT concept_id, concept_code
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.cms_synthetic_patient_data_omop.concept`
  WHERE vocabulary_id='ICD10CM' AND concept_code IN ('L70','L20','L40','L80')
),
descendants AS (
  SELECT r.concept_code AS root_code, ca.descendant_concept_id
  FROM roots AS r
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.cms_synthetic_patient_data_omop.concept_ancestor` ca
    ON ca.ancestor_concept_id = r.concept_id
),
root_counts AS (
  SELECT d.root_code,
         COUNT(DISTINCT co.person_id) AS n_persons
  FROM descendants d
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.cms_synthetic_patient_data_omop.condition_occurrence` co
    ON co.condition_concept_id = d.descendant_concept_id
  GROUP BY d.root_code
),
total AS (
  SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT person_id) AS tot
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.cms_synthetic_patient_data_omop.person`
)
SELECT rc.root_code,
       rc.n_persons,
       t.tot,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(rc.n_persons, t.tot)*100 AS pct_participants
FROM root_counts rc CROSS JOIN total t
ORDER BY root_code;
